From: Arjune <arjunevaibhavpatil1434@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: rockchip: rk3288: keep timer7 running if already started

timer7 drives the architected counter on RK3288. rockchip_timer_init()
always stops and reloads it, which resets the counter. Under Xen this
makes Xen's system time jump backwards, its timers never fire and dom0
hangs at its first sleep (~2 s into boot, gmac PHY reset).

U-Boot's TPL/SPL already start timer7 and skip re-initialisation when it
is enabled; do the same here.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rockchip.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rockchip.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rockchip.c	2026-10-23 21:29:09.890365868 +0530
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rockchip.c	2026-10-23 21:29:09.910365909 +0530
@@ -35,11 +35,18 @@
 		 */
 		reg_base = ioremap(RK3288_TIMER6_7_PHYS, SZ_16K);
 		if (reg_base) {
-			writel(0, reg_base + 0x30);
-			writel(0xffffffff, reg_base + 0x20);
-			writel(0xffffffff, reg_base + 0x24);
-			writel(1, reg_base + 0x30);
-			dsb();
+			/*
+			 * Leave timer7 alone if the bootloader already started
+			 * it: reloading it resets the architected counter,
+			 * which breaks a hypervisor (Xen) running below us.
+			 */
+			if (!(readl(reg_base + 0x30) & 1)) {
+				writel(0, reg_base + 0x30);
+				writel(0xffffffff, reg_base + 0x20);
+				writel(0xffffffff, reg_base + 0x24);
+				writel(1, reg_base + 0x30);
+				dsb();
+			}
 			iounmap(reg_base);
 		} else {
 			pr_err("rockchip: could not map timer7 registers\n");
